\label{thmfunctionalrelations}
	Let $({\cal C}, J)$ be a small-generated site. Then, for any presheaves $P,Q\in [{\cal C}^{\textup{op}},{\bf Set }]$, the arrows $a_{J}(P)\to a_{J}(Q)$ in ${\bf Sh}({\cal C}, J)$ are in natural bijection with the $J$-functional relations from $P$ to $Q$ in $[{\cal C}^{\textup{op}},{\bf Set }]$.

	Moreover, under this bijection, the composition of arrows in ${\bf Sh}({\cal C}, J)$ corresponds to the $c_{J}$-closure of the composition in $[{\cal C}^{\textup{op}},{\bf Set }]$ of the associated $J$-functional relations. This operation, which we shall denote by the symbol $\ast$, admits the following explicit description: given a $J$-functional relation $R$ from $P$ to $Q$ and a $J$-functional relation $S$ from $Q$ to $Z$, $S\ast R$ is given by the formula
	\begin{equation*}\begin{split}
	(S\ast R)(c)&=\{(x, z)\in P(c)\times Z(c) \mid \{f:d\to c \mid \exists y\in Q(d)\, \\
	& \quad\quad(P(f)(x), y)\in R(d)\textup{ and } (y, Z(f)(z))\in S(d)\}\in J(c) \}
	\end{split}\end{equation*}
	for any $c\in {\cal C}$.

\begin{equation*}\begin{split}
	(S\ast R)(c)&=\{(x, z)\in P(c)\times Z(c) \mid \{f:d\to c \mid \exists y\in Q(d)\, \\
	& \quad\quad(P(f)(x), y)\in R(d)\textup{ and } (y, Z(f)(z))\in S(d)\}\in J(c) \}
	\end{split}\end{equation*}

