\label{propadjointinduction}
	Let $({\cal C}, J)$ and $({\cal D}, K)$ be small-generated sites, and $F:{\cal C}\to {\cal D}\dashv G:{\cal D}\to {\cal C}$ adjoint functors. Then
	\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
		\item $F$ has the covering-lifting property if and only if $G$ is cover-preserving.

		\item $G$ is a morphism of sites $({\cal D}, T_{\cal D})\to ({\cal C}, T_{\cal C})$, where $T_{\cal C}$ and $T_{\cal D}$ are the trivial topologies respectively on $\cal C$ and $\cal D$, and induces an essential geometric morphism $[{\cal C}^{\textup{op}}, {\bf Set }]\to [{\cal D}^{\textup{op}}, {\bf Set }]$;

		\item $G$ is a morphism of sites $({\cal D}, K) \to ({\cal C}, J)$ (equivalently, by (i), $G$ is cover-preserving) if and only if $F$ is a comorphism of sites $({\cal C}, J)\to ({\cal D}, K)$.

		\item In the situation of (iii), the geometric morphism $C_{F}$ induced by $F$ co-incides with the geometric morphism ${\bf Sh}(G)$ induced by $G$.
	\end{enumerate}

