\label{remcorrelationcomorphisms}
	\begin{enumerate}[(a)]
		\item The property that $F$ be a comorphism of sites $({\cal D}, K)\to ({\cal C}, J)$ is not only a necessary but also a sufficient condition for $\pi_{\cal C}'$ to be a comorphism of sites. Notice the analogy with Remark \ref{remcorrelationmorphisms}. 

		\item The canonical projection functor $\pi_{\cal C}':(F \downarrow 1_{\cal C}) \to {\cal C}$ is a split fibration, corresponding to the internal category in $[{\cal C}^{\textup{op}}, {\bf Set }]$ given by $c \mapsto (F(c)\downarrow {\cal D})$.

